MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ad496817cc2ac7b498b32f0fc2de6fb3, type: 3}
  m_Name: R1_08_HeartOfTheForest
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalEntry
  title: "8 \xB7 Heart of the Forest"
  pages:
  - bigIdea: Impulse adds momentum. Every hit on the paddle hands the flywheel the
      crate's momentum.
    notes: 'The Momentum Engine at last! The flywheel stores momentum: each time
      the crate slams into its paddle, the crate''s momentum moves into the wheel.
      A few good hits in a row and it really gets going.'
    lookCloser: "Burst: \u0394v = 15 \xF7 2 = 7.5 m/s for the 2 kg crate.\nOver the
      wet track it keeps \u2248 <color=#896923>14 kg\xB7m/s</color> and hands it
      to the wheel.\nFull speed: 50 kg\xB7m/s, about four or five hits."
    funFact: Real flywheels store energy in factories, trains and even some race
      cars, spinning thousands of times a minute.
    marginP1: Hit, pull, hit, pull...
    marginP2: Faster! It's slowing down!
    diagram:
      show: 1
      objectLabel: 'Crate

        2 kg'
      forces:
      - label: Burst
        newtons: 15
        direction: 0
        kind: 5
        unit: "N\xB7s"
      caption: "One Burst: 15 kg\xB7m/s, nearly all of it into the wheel."
    sketch: {fileID: 0}
  - bigIdea: Friction slowly takes momentum away, and the Bearing keeps that loss
      small.
    notes: 'Without the Bearing the wheel''s axle would grind, and it would lose
      its momentum almost as fast as you add it. With it, the wheel loses only a
      little each second. That slow loss is your clock: the gate stays open while
      the wheel still has enough momentum.'
    lookCloser: "Friction: <color=#7d3029>1.5 kg\xB7m/s</color> lost each second.\nThe
      gate needs 35. From a full 50: (50 \u2212 35) \xF7 1.5 = 10 seconds to get
      through."
    funFact: 'Ball bearings are everywhere: bikes, skateboards, fans, hard drives.
      Less friction, longer spin.'
    marginP1: Ten seconds. Easy.
    marginP2: Famous last words. RUN!
    diagram:
      show: 0
      objectLabel: 2 kg
      forces: []
      caption: 
    sketch: {fileID: 0}
  - bigIdea: 'Weight and balance, one last time: the heavier side goes down and lifts
      the other.'
    notes: The Counterweight hangs on the far pan. It weighs more than both of you
      together, so when you release the brake it sinks and carries you up to the
      Great Shard.
    lookCloser: 'Counterweight (3 kg): <color=#8a5a2e>88.3 N</color>    Both of you:
      <color=#8a5a2e>58.9 N</color>

      Net <color=#a26029>29.4 N</color>, minus
      a little pulley friction: up you go.'
    funFact: 'Every lesson in the Shattered Grounds, all in one machine: force, mass,
      friction, momentum, weight, balance.'
    marginP1: We built a whole engine.
    marginP2: Wren is going to cry.
    diagram:
      show: 1
      objectLabel: Lift
      forces:
      - label: Counterweight
        newtons: 88.3
        direction: 1
        kind: 1
        unit: N
      - label: You two
        newtons: 58.9
        direction: 0
        kind: 1
        unit: N
      caption: '88.3 N beats 58.9 N: the counterweight sinks, you rise.'
    sketch: {fileID: 0}
  tip: 'Install the parts, then keep a rhythm: one of you Bursts the crate into the
    paddle, the other pulls it back from the perch. When the gate opens, run! Behind
    it, both of you on the pan, then pull the lever.'
  sketch: {fileID: 0}
  sketchCaption: 
